{"id": "67:13", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "et speciéi domus divídere spólia", "portuguese": "e à beleza da casa cabe repartir os despojos", "problem": "'cabe' supplies a full verb (it falls to / it is proper), which interprets the bare dative + infinitive more than a copula would. The Latin leaves the construction elliptical.", "fix": "e à beleza da casa, repartir os despojos"}]},
{"id": "67:15", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "nive dealbabúntur in Selmon", "portuguese": "ficarão brancos de neve no Selmon", "problem": "The Latin future passive ('they will be whitened') becomes a resultative 'ficarão brancos', so the voice is lost.", "fix": "serão embranquecidos de neve no Selmon"}]},
{"id": "67:20", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Deus salutárium nostrórum", "portuguese": "o Deus da nossa salvação", "problem": "'salutarium' is plural ('of our salvations'), and the translation makes it singular, which changes the number.", "fix": "o Deus das nossas salvações"}]},
{"id": "67:24", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "lingua canum tuórum ex inimícis, ab ipso", "portuguese": "a língua dos teus cães, dos inimigos, dele mesmo", "problem": "'ex inimicis' means 'from/out of the enemies'. Placed in apposition, the bare 'dos inimigos' reads as a possessive, so the dogs seem to be the enemies. The preposition's sense of source is lost.", "fix": "a língua dos teus cães, a partir dos inimigos, dele mesmo"}]},
{"id": "67:28a", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "in mentis excéssu", "portuguese": "fora de si", "problem": "In ordinary Portuguese, 'fora de si' usually means enraged or out of control. The Latin 'excess of mind' is ecstasy or rapture, and the translation also drops the concrete 'mentis'.", "fix": "em êxtase da mente"}]},
{"id": "67:36", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "benedíctus Deus", "portuguese": "bendito seja Deus", "problem": "'seja' makes the verbless Latin optative. Elsewhere in this psalm the same formula is left without a verb (67:20 'Bendito o Senhor'), so the mood is resolved here and inconsistently.", "fix": "bendito Deus"}]}
], "overall": "A faithful, close rendering that keeps the Septuagintal oddities of this very obscure psalm (cleros as 'partilhas', mons coagulatus, speciei domus, the gen. patris orphanorum agreeing with ejus) instead of smoothing them toward the Hebrew. No critical or major faults were found, and the pointing marks match the Latin in every verse. The remaining points are minor: voice in 67:15, number in 67:20, the force of 'ex' in 67:24, the connotation of 'fora de si', and the supplied verbs 'cabe' and 'seja'."}
